WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Where do earthworms go on a hot, dry day?

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.900
After rain, you may find them under a log.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.280
With a baking tray, you and your child can see which conditions the worms move

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.280
toward.

5
00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:17.573
Allow about thirty-five minutes once you have your worms.

6
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:23.213
Your child practices looking closely, making a prediction, and checking it.

7
00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:28.553
You’ll change one thing at a time, count where the worms go, and repeat the test.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:33.883
Start with six to ten earthworms from a bait shop or a damp garden bed.

9
00:00:35.123 --> 00:00:36.283
Stay with your child throughout.

10
00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.703
You do the digging.

11
00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:43.403
Keep the worms in damp soil in the shade and use them that day.

12
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.877
Have children stand back about six feet.

13
00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:51.317
Tilt the log or rock toward you with a stick so it shields you.

14
00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:55.197
Never touch snakes or animals that bite or sting.

15
00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:59.297
Never taste outdoor plants, berries, or mushrooms.

16
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.000
A thrashing worm with a smooth, milky-white band may be a jumping worm.

17
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.580
Leave it and its soil there.

18
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.480
Take a photo and ask your local Extension office.

19
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.900
Keep worms, bits of soil, pebbles, and plastic wrap away from children under four.

20
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.200
Call nine one one if someone is choking.

21
00:01:22.383 --> 00:01:24.443
Wet your hands and your child’s.

22
00:01:24.443 --> 00:01:27.603
Never squeeze or drop a worm.

23
00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:31.723
Watch one on a damp paper towel for a minute or two.

24
00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:34.463
Ask, "Which end is the front?"

25
00:01:34.463 --> 00:01:36.203
The band is near the front.

26
00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:38.663
You may hear bristles scratch.

27
00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:41.697
Line the tray with paper towels.

28
00:01:43.037 --> 00:01:44.077
Keep one half dry.

29
00:01:45.357 --> 00:01:48.957
Dampen the other with plain water, stopping before puddles form.

30
00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:53.257
Ask, "Which side will the worms go to, damp or dry?"

31
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.460
Place the worms across the middle line.

32
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.420
Cover the whole tray with cardboard so both sides are equally dark.

33
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.580
After ten minutes, count each side.

34
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.400
Count any worm on the line as middle.

35
00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:11.923
Suppose six of eight worms end up on the damp left side.

36
00:02:13.263 --> 00:02:16.343
Imagine turning the tray so the damp half is on the right.

37
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:20.243
Where do you predict most worms will end up this time?

38
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.147
Turn the tray around.

39
00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:31.607
Ask, "Do you think more worms will end up on the damp side again?"

40
00:02:32.307 --> 00:02:34.847
Return the worms to the middle and cover the tray.

41
00:02:36.187 --> 00:02:37.727
After ten minutes, count again.

42
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.507
Add the damp counts together, then the dry counts.

43
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:45.970
Earthworms breathe through their skin, which has to stay moist.

44
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.170
Most move away from dry ground and bright light toward damp, dark places.

45
00:02:52.317 --> 00:02:55.497
For the optional light test, dampen the tray evenly.

46
00:02:56.857 --> 00:02:58.077
Keep it out of direct sun.

47
00:02:59.417 --> 00:03:02.057
Cover half with cardboard and half with a clear lid.

48
00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:04.497
Use bright room light.

49
00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:10.097
Or set a cool LED lamp about two feet above the clear half, away from water.

50
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:12.823
Earthworms have no eyes.

51
00:03:14.103 --> 00:03:15.303
Their skin senses light.

52
00:03:16.623 --> 00:03:17.643
Predict where they’ll go.

53
00:03:18.823 --> 00:03:19.943
Start them in the middle.

54
00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:23.463
Cover both halves to keep them equally damp.

55
00:03:24.643 --> 00:03:26.043
Count after ten minutes.

56
00:03:27.503 --> 00:03:29.883
Swap covers, move the lamp if used, and repeat.

57
00:03:30.967 --> 00:03:33.047
Mist yard worms with plain water.

58
00:03:34.587 --> 00:03:37.267
Return them to damp soil in the shade where you found them.

59
00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.367
Watch them burrow.

60
00:03:40.547 --> 00:03:42.567
Never release bait-shop worms outdoors.

61
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:45.647
Wash your hands with soap and water.
